WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.506
What makes something an agent?

00:00:02.606 --> 00:00:04.484
It comes down to one question.

00:00:04.584 --> 00:00:09.822
Who decides what happens next? The human, your code, or the model?

00:00:11.022 --> 00:00:14.460
An agent is an app that plans and acts toward a goal.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:21.990
The model is its brain. Tools are its hands. Orchestration, its nervous system.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.854
Deployment, its body.

00:00:24.404 --> 00:00:28.514
And it runs one loop: think, act, observe.

00:00:29.064 --> 00:00:32.910
Around the model sit five layers, each answering one question.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:40.257
Context: what it sees. The loop: who decides. The gate: who sorts.

00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:45.040
The harness: what it can reach. Evals: how you know.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:49.220
And a failure in one layer wears the mask of another.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:55.344
So, agent or workflow? Ask one thing. Can you write down the steps?

00:00:55.444 --> 00:00:57.178
If you can, write them.

00:00:57.728 --> 00:01:03.854
Agents use about four times the tokens of a chat. Multi-agent systems, about fifteen.

00:01:04.404 --> 00:01:10.098
That's module zero, the map. Start with page one: What an agent is.
